Generated changelog for v1.9.0

--- Technical ---
### Changed

- This release will integrate the M9 - Frontend Redesign milestone into `main` and add the v1.9.0 release notes. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- This release will add inline citation badges anchored in the assistant Markdown answer. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- This release will add a primary action button from `SuggestedNextSteps`. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- This release will add a keyboard-first command palette that opens over any page on `Ctrl+K`. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- This release will add optimistic status updates with rollback on the board and detail views. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- This release will replace dialog-based status and assignee edits with inline popovers anchored to the header actions. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- This release will add inline citation badges with hover preview in the assistant chat. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- This release will inject the agent roster into the system prompt for the assistant. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- This release will enforce the grounding check via `tool_choice` in the assistant. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- This release will introduce a single source for the design tokens, including spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic color. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- This release will fix the board card title wrapping so that `-webkit-line-clamp` is not blockified. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- This release will fix the assistant composer send button to sit inside its panel. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- This release will fix the `Category` header overlapping `Due` in the ticket queue. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- This release will update the assistant's system prompt to include a confirmation policy for write-honesty and no needless confirmation. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- This release will render summary timestamps in the user's timezone. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- This release will report failed knowledge-base searches as errors. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- This release will score grounding by meaning, not word overlap, using a semantic similarity approach. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))
